CRITICAL 3D PRINTER SAFETY, THERMAL RUNAWAY & FIRE HAZARD DISCLAIMER:
================================================================================

1. HIGH-TEMPERATURE THERMAL HAZARDS:
   3D printers contain high-current electrical heating elements, heated print
   beds, extruders, and stepper motors operating at extreme temperatures
   (exceeding 200°C–300°C / 400°F–570°F). Improper control, electrical failure,
   hardware malfunction, serial communication drops, power interruptions, or
   software errors can cause thermal runaway, electrical shorts, equipment
   meltdown, structural fire, property damage, serious personal injury, or death.

2. UNATTENDED OPERATION HAZARD:
   NEVER LEAVE A 3D PRINTER OPERATING UNATTENDED. Always maintain an operable
   smoke detector and an appropriate Class B/C fire extinguisher in the vicinity
   of the printer.

